# tilt_cal.jsc - end-to-end tilt mapping: synthetic BMI270 -> TiltController -> final stick.
# The synthetic IMU is held at the 35 deg pose; tilt angles are relative to it (see
# tools/sim/synth_imu.h). Assist Pro removes the ring magnet, so turn/climb = tilt output.
# Checks (group D, DESIGN.md section 21):
#   roll +15 -> turn > 0.4 | roll -15 -> turn < -0.4 | roll 2 -> turn == 0
#   top toward the face (pitch -10) -> climb > 0 | invert flips it
#   recalibrating at a new hold pose zeroes the output
# The synthetic IMU runs noise-free here (the gyro bias stays): roll +15 deg maps to turn 0.409
# at Med, so the 0.4 threshold has only ~0.4 deg of margin, less than the calibration error the
# section 18 noise causes. `jetsim --selftest` repeats the mapping with noise (tilt[B]).
0     imu noise off
0     persist assist 2
0     state title             # the boot CALIBRATE state calibrates at the hold pose
+0    assert calibrated == 1
+0    state free
+0.2  seek sea 60
+0.3  tilt 2 0 0.2
+1.0  assert turn == 0
+0    assert tilt_valid == 1
+0    tilt 15 0 0.3
+1.5  assert turn > 0.4
+0    tilt -15 0 0.3
+1.5  assert turn < -0.4
+0    tilt 0 -10 0.3
+1.5  assert climb > 0
+0    tap I                   # invert pitch
+0.5  assert climb < 0
+0    tap I                   # back to normal
+0.5  assert climb > 0
+0    tilt 0 0 0.3
+1.0  assert climb == 0
+0    assert turn == 0
+0    seek sea 60
+0.1  pose 55 0.5             # new hold pose: 20 deg further toward the face
+1.0  assert climb > 0.3      # reads as a strong climb until recalibrated
+0    tap C                   # recalibrate (0.5 s, game paused)
+2.0  assert calibrated == 1
+0    assert turn == 0
+0    assert climb == 0
+0    end
